== Description ==
Three-quarters of Nordaustlandet is covered by glaciers, the largest being Austfonna at 7,000 square kilometres (2,700 sq mi). The landscape has low, rounded hills and plains, created by glaciation during former ice ages. Most of the reserve has little or no vegetation, and the reserve belongs to the polar desert. The nature reserve is used by scientists and tourists, the latter...","coordinates":[{"lat":79,"lon":23,"primary":true,"globe":"earth"}],"pageimage":"Nordaustlandet_(js)_2.jpg","pageprops":{"page_image_free":"Nordaustlandet_(js)_2.jpg","wikibase-shortdesc":"Nature reserve in Svalbard, Norway","wikibase_item":"Q1361777"}}]}}
